{"id": "EUVD-2026-45766", "enisaUuid": "8d37b10f-2515-3302-9203-7a95aeadc7dd", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amdkfd: fix a vulnerability of integer overflow in kfd debugger\n\nget_queue_ids() computes array_size = num_queues * sizeof(uint32_t),\nwhich could overflow on 32-bit size_t build. using array_size()\ninstead, it saturates to SIZE_MAX on overflow.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 2d57a0475f085c08b49312dfd8edcb461845f285)", "datePublished": "2026-07-19T14:54:53", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T20:17:54", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4e5f808b454167cc58d7084a407a554d8ddc694d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/de70a80992396ee306ee3a2810ad28aa1608ba9b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5cf4a41aa0d74e4c83f82d2ce233b5189ed4b43c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4f9eeedc3d3151f8a226fd676c314a813edda5a1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/93f5534b35a05ef8a0109c1eefa800062fee810a"], "aliases": ["GHSA-pg6j-5v22-gvqf", "CVE-2026-63881"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.19, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0ae6a3cd-33d1-3089-96f6-71e9659f40a3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a70a93fa568b4f05aba548dadb673703eccf5480 <de70a80992396ee306ee3a2810ad28aa1608ba9b"}, {"id": "2353be44-1a7e-3192-a8cd-997ccc1343b1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.0.12"}, {"id": "6ea81573-d052-3c41-858e-c7b49b03012a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a70a93fa568b4f05aba548dadb673703eccf5480 <4e5f808b454167cc58d7084a407a554d8ddc694d"}, {"id": "736fa7b2-34d2-3464-b486-b3844c8a7303", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "869593b1-931d-39da-a3b7-c854fde3cd49", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "p